 "text": "Hey there, how are you? A thin oil painting usually needs about four to six weeks, and a thicker one about eight to ten. Even with a little patience, it'll look much better. Oils dry from the top down, so let the top finish, where the brush marks are, dry first. Run your finger over it, and if it doesn't leave a trace, it's dry. Some oils take a full year to cure, so keep that in mind.",
